# The build context is docker/, which both images share for the guard, and only what this image
# needs goes in. Anything not named below stays out, so a target/ folder, a local config, a
# certificate or a key never reaches the build. The guard's tests are left out too: the image
# builds the guard without them.
*
!relay/relay.toml
!relay/open.toml
!guard/Cargo.toml
!guard/Cargo.lock
!guard/src
guard/src/tests.rs
guard/src/tests
